<title>USA: Sholodge Inc Q4 net rises.</title>
<headline>Sholodge Inc Q4 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>GALLATIN, Tenn. 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unaudited Financial Highlights</p>
<p>		    (In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>			    Fourth Quarter Ended  Fiscal Year Ended</p>
<p>			     12/29/96  12/31/95  12/29/96  12/31/95</p>
<p> Hotel operating revenues  $13,136  $10,021 $57,528   $44,144</p>
<p> Total operating revenues   14,465   12,107  63,483    78,620</p>
<p>Net income from continuing</p>
<p>operations before</p>
<p>  extraordinary items	  1,421    1,139   9,497    17,760</p>
<p>Earnings (Loss) from</p>
<p>discontinued</p>
<p>  operations/a			 -     (53)	 -	(75)</p>
<p> Extraordinary items/b	     -	(9)	 -     (708)</p>
<p> Net income			1,421    1,077   9,497    16,977</p>
<p>Net income per share (Primary):</p>
<p>    Net income		    0.17     0.13    1.13	1.99</p>
<p>Net income per share</p>
<p>(Fully Diluted):</p>
<p>    Net income		    0.17     0.13    1.12	1.80</p>
<p>Average shares outstanding:</p>
<p>    Primary			8,401    8,342   8,441     8,526</p>
<p>    Fully diluted	     10,718   10,658  10,764    10,842</p>
<p>NOTE: The company sold its 60 percent ownership interest in its restaurant operations effective December 31, 1995.</p>
<p>Extraordinary items represent primarily noncash charges net of income taxes resulting from the early extinguishment of indebtedness in 1995.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
